            <ArticleTitle>Stress myocardial perfusion imaging after coronary angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>766-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Stress myocardial perfusion imaging is useful in patient management after coronary angioplasty. The ischemic perfusion pattern suggests the presence of residual stenosis, restenosis, down stream stenosis, side branch stenosis, and remote stenosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
